2 questions we need to answer:
Reliability - Does the model agree with itself over multiple runs (is it hallucinating)?
Validity - Does the model agree with the Ground Truth (assessors check).

Good LLM is reliable (no deviation between runs) and match Ground Truth (assessors check).
Reliability (Fleiss' kappa) tells us whether it repeats itself; validity (accuracy vs. human experts) tells us whether it's right.

 Kappa answers reliability only — "is it consistent."  "is it correct." That's acc_gt (accuracy vs. the human experts). The best model is
  the one that is high on both:

Claude is the most reliable (kappa 0.67) and the most valid (acc_gt 0.84)
